    "sha": "025f59e362eca56497a976205b960958cab3caf5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV5OD-doAKDAyNWY1OWUzNjJlY2E1NjQ5N2E5NzYyMDViOTYwOTU4Y2FiM2NhZjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T13:33:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T13:33:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): the stock export judges the mesh as the file holds it; weld settles duplicates by edge parity\n\nBinary STL writes each corner as f32, so corners closer than one f32 step\nare one corner in the file and a mesh that passed the closed check in f64\nwas written with repeated corners and edges not on two facets.\nstock_export::file_bytes rounds to the written values (repair::weld_at_f32);\nwhen a facet collapses there it welds bit-exact and checks the result with\nunpaired_edges, refusing by name. A mesh with nothing to collapse writes\nbyte for byte as before. The UI's stock export and write_stl use it.\n\nrepair::drop_degenerate kept one copy of a back-to-back pair, which left its\nthree edges odd. Duplicates now keep no copy when the rest of the mesh uses\neach of their edges an even number of times, and the first copy otherwise\n(a stray copy on a closed solid, as pinned before).\n\nFixes #4182\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
